## 1 The 17 disposition rows

1a Row 1 (may_remove): fixed. 10.3.3 now reads `anyone_in_conversations_it_started` with the ruled wording and a v0.1 note. 1b Row 2 (C-17): fixed. Class table ends at C-16; new 10.2.2.a keeps custody release inside C-10 / break-glass (R-80.a (7)); OP-3 carries the ruling-change note. 1c Row 3 (C-9c): fixed. 10.3.2.e constrains renewal to grant records (every rule `start`/`resume`, identical body, unexpired); 10.3.2.e.3 states budget never resets [P]. 1d Row 4 (C-15): fixed. One event and one digest per account; batch form withdrawn with the ruling cited in C-15 and OP-1. 1e Row 5 (digest): fixed. 10.3.2.c removes both `digest` and `signature`; 10.3.2.c.5 binds the authorising event to the unapproved form; the profile example carries an approval; 10.3.5 refuses empty `approvals`. 1f Row 6 (format): fixed per 2c below. 1g Row 7 (PH-3 exit): fixed. 6.2.4.c (2) tests C-2a/C-6a live and C-10 by fixture, live at PH-4 exit (6.2.5.c (9)). 1h Row 8 (pilot): fixed. A0 moved to PH-3 behind the C-15 route, consistently in 6.2.3.a, 6.2.4.a (12)/c (5), 6.5.2, 4.2, 9.2/9.3; no new RA needed. 1i Row 9: fixed as disposed — SI-15 closed in PH-1 by the estate guard (3.3.1.d, X4); SI-7 on old rails is RA-9 (11.3.9) + OP-23 (13.2.16), cited in 3.3.1.e and the SI-7 row. 1j Row 10: OP-21 (13.2.14), options A–D, recommendation A; BV-5 aligned and marked pending; CX-2 points at it — not decided. 1k Row 11: OP-22 (13.2.15); 6.6 and 15.5.5 point at it — not decided. 1l Row 12: fixed. 6.2.1.d keeps the recorder, off switch removed with a v0.1 note. 1m Row 13: fixed. Six item-by-item PH-6 procedures (6.2.7.c), D-1 note, 6.8.3, re-render in 16.2/16.4. 1n Row 14: fixed. RA-4 ends in two separately stated parts (11.3.4.d.1–d.3). 1o Row 15: fixed. OP-10 A names the five rules 3.1.b–3.1.f. 1p Row 16: fixed. The plaintext-content-field baseline is in 6.2.1.a (2) and exit (4). 1q Row 17: fixed. 4.4.c and 11.2 now say "every other P1 delivery item" with the two later exceptions named. No row unfixed o